WHAT THE PILOT DECIDES
  Current yield is 0.66 informative cases per group (2,853 from 4,326),
  measured on PARTIAL groups -- the old sample only held renderings from
  sampled filers. Corpus-first groups are complete, so yield should rise,
  but by how much is exactly what cannot be assumed.

  At 0.66/group, 50,000 cases needs ~75,800 groups. Reading that off the
  table above at the cheap end (sizes 2 and 3-4) puts the full run near
  5.8 hours; drawn at the universe average it is far more.
  The pilot replaces both of those arithmetic guesses with a measurement.
